rings, not in the plan: mypy's incremental cache is discarded every run (a TESTAMENT=off local run is always cold), and the /usr/local/lib/mypy fallback is reported missing. The release.yml premise is the one alignment miss (see the release-gate finding). Each why is recorded, and none needs a ruling beyond the owner's review.", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-typecheck-on-the-pool.md"], "fid": "R-14"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Cross-checks: no learnings corpus; backlog cache empty and 7 days old; Records Pass covered the one oracle file", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Learnings Cross-Check: `prawduct-hook learnings-files --for-diff` printed nothing (exit 0), and .claude/rules/learnings/ does not exist, so no rule applied and none was added this cycle. Backlog Reconciliation: `cache-query affecting` over the changed files, `search typecheck`, `search mypy` and `open` each returned 0 items, from a cache last confirmed 2026-11-11 (7 days old), so nothing appears resolved. C-B4: the plan's '#1278' resolves to no cached item; it names a PR run, not a backlog item, so no action is needed. Records Pass covered files_oracle = {.prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-typecheck-on-the-pool.md}. Its line 50 release.yml claim clears the 'misleads into action' bar and is folded into the release-gate finding. No other claim in it clears a bar: the 32-package/33-root count is inert. priors: rev-20261112T035922Z R-3 (check-all reading every exit 2 as 'testament gave no verdict') applies equally to the new typecheck branch at scripts/check-all.sh:13-19,81-83. A local pytest collection error in typecheck/ exits 2 and is reported as no verdict. The same accepted reason holds (the runbook names the other exit-2 sources, and the gate still fails), so it is not re-raised.", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-typecheck-on-the-pool.md", "scripts/check-all.sh"], "fid": "R-15"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 8, "note": 7}, "observ